@startuml
title PayLink - UNKNOWN payment later confirmed COMPLETED (UC16, US-13.3, US-14, US-26.4)
' Names follow docs/design/glossary.md and docs/design/architecture.md.
' Transition 7 of the brief section 2.5: UNKNOWN -> COMPLETED.
' Only `payments` orchestrates, only `accounts` writes the ledger.

skinparam shadowing false
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign left
autonumber

actor "SupportUser" as Support
participant "ReconciliationService" as Rec
participant "BillerAdapter" as Ad
participant "PaymentService" as PS
participant "WalletService" as Wal
participant "AuditLog" as Audit
participant "NotificationObserver" as Notif

note over PS
  Start state: payment is UNKNOWN, the hold is still ACTIVE.
  No refund was made (UNKNOWN is never refunded automatically).
end note

alt a re-query (after 1, 5 or 15 minutes) or a callback gets CONFIRMED
  Ad -> PS : onBillerResult(reference, CONFIRMED)
else the settlement file lists the payment as paid (US-26.4)
  Rec -> PS : onBillerResult(reference, CONFIRMED)
else support confirms by hand (UC16, US-13.3)
  Support -> PS : resolveUnknown(paymentId, CONFIRMED, actor)
  PS -> Audit : insert(actor, "resolveUnknown", reason, refId = paymentId)
end

PS -> PS : check status is UNKNOWN (else ignore and log)
PS -> PS : status COMPLETED, write history (UNKNOWN -> COMPLETED)
PS -> Wal : captureHold(HoldId)
Wal -> Wal : Hold ACTIVE -> CAPTURED
Wal -> Wal : LedgerEntry DEBIT (held_delta = -total)
Wal -> Wal : LedgerEntry FEE_INCOME (SYSTEM wallet, fee_amount)
opt an agent was involved (D-10)
  Wal -> Wal : LedgerEntry COMMISSION (agent wallet, 40% of the fee)
  Wal -> Wal : save Commission(paymentId, agent, amount)
end
Wal -> Audit : insert(one row per ledger entry, refId = ledger entry id) (NFR-05)
Wal --> PS : done

PS ->> Notif : onPaymentEvent(PaymentEvent COMPLETED)
note right of Notif
  Customer gets the success message.
  A failed send is retried 3 times and never changes the payment.
end note

note over PS, Wal
  The fee of the payment was fixed when the payment was created
  (FeeCalculator at that day), so the amounts are the same as in a
  payment that was CONFIRMED at once (seq-pay-bill.puml).
end note
@enduml
